: 50px; width: 83.425px;\">1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 102.637px;\">M6</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 125.35px;\">7</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 241.488px;\">12.5</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 83.425px;\">1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 102.637px;\">M8</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 125.35px;\">9</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 241.488px;\">12.5</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 83.425px;\">1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 102.637px;\">Handle</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 125.35px;\">6.5</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 241.488px;\">34</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"text-align: center; height: 50px; width: 83.425px;\">1</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
  "description_text": "Printed plastic threads can wear out or strip over time, especially in parts that are assembled and disassembled repeatedly. Brass heat-set inserts provide durable metal threads, helping improve assembly strength and making printed parts more suitable for repeated fastening.\n\nThe 100W USB‑C Smart Soldering Iron Kit includes two custom tips designed specifically for heat-set insert installation, allowing inserts to be installed directly with fast heating and accurate control. This provides a cleaner and more reliable way to add threaded metal fastening points to printed parts.\n\nThe included heat-insert tooling supports common insert sizes used in 3D printing, including M2, M2.5, M3, M4, M5, M6, and M8. This makes it easier to handle a wide range of printed enclosures, brackets, and functional assemblies.\n\nCompared with using a standard soldering tip directly, dedicated insert tips help guide heat-set inserts more steadily during installation. This reduces the risk of tilting, slipping, or uneven insertion, which is especially important for printed parts that require accurate alignment and secure fastening.\n\nWith USB‑C PD/QC input, the soldering iron supports fast heat-up and accurate temperature control in a compact form factor. A temperature range of 100–450°C ±5°C and a heat-up time of 2 seconds at 100W make it suitable for both soldering tasks and heat-insert installation.\n\n3D Model\n\nIncludes a 3D model file of the soldering iron for holder or fixture design.",
